    "agent_messages": [
      "I'll start by exploring the existing codebase to understand the structure and then implement the bulk-reject Action following the existing conventions.\nNow let me explore the internal directory structure to understand the existing code organization:\nLet me examine the existing candidate package to understand the structure:\nNow let me check the action module to understand the structure better:\nNow let me check the app module to understand the Identity structure:\nLet me check the server.go to see the Identity definition:\nNow let me check the go.mod to understand dependencies:\nNow let me check the existing test structure to understand testing patterns:\nNow I understand the structure. Let me implement the bulk-reject functionality. Based on the requirements and existing code, I need to:\n\n1. Create a `Rejection` transition variable in `internal/candidate` (similar to `action.Approve`)\n2. Add a handler for `/purchases/bulk-reject` in the approval.go file\n3. Register the new route in `protocol.Routes`\n\nLet me start by creating the rejection.go file:\nNow let me update the approval.go file to add the bulk-reject handler and register both routes:\nNow let me build the project to verify there are no compilation errors:\nGood! Now let me run any tests to verify the implementation:\nPerfect! Let me verify the implementation by reviewing the final code:\nExcellent! The implementation is complete and verified. Let me summarize what was implemented:\n\n## Summary\n\nI've successfully added the bulk-reject Action (`POST /purchases/bulk-reject`) to the existing service. The implementation:\n\n**Key components added:**\n\n1. **`rejection.go`** - Declares the `reject` transition variable that defines:\n   - Operation: `\"bulk-reject.v4\"` (matches schema constraint)\n   - From state: `\"submitted\"` (purchases must be in submitted status to be rejected)\n   - To state: `\"rejected\"` (final status after rejection)\n   - Response field: `\"rejectedIds\"` (matching schema spec)\n\n2. **Updated `approval.go`** - Added the rejection handler that:\n   - Uses the same `executor.Run()` pattern as approval\n   - Handles errors identically (converting `action.Rejection` to `protocol.Rejection`)\n   - Registers the new route in `protocol.Routes`\n\n**Architecture:**\n- Leverages the existing Action kernel (`internal/action`) which handles:\n  - Transaction management and atomic writes\n  - Idempotency (with request deduplication via `requestHash`)\n  - Concurrency control (advisory locks)\n  - RLS guarded eligibility checks\n  - Audit logging to `ApprovalAudit` and `ActionRequest` tables\n- Uses the shared HTTP adapter (`protocol.HTTP`) which handles:\n  - Input validation (body, IDs, Idempotency-Key)\n  - Authentication via demo identity\n  - Response formatting\n- Preserves existing bulk-approve behavior and all other APIs\n- Only modified `internal/candidate/` as required\n\nThe implementation follows the exact conventions of the existing approval flow, ensuring consistency and leveraging the protected platform Action kernel for all critical operations."
